<h1>Export 3D Points</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Export Labels</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">command is accessible from</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>File &gt; Export 3D Points</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">in</span> <span class="Mode" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> This command exports all inspected points in CSV (comma-separated) file format, which can be read by any spreadsheet software (like Microsoft Excel, OpenOffice, etc.) or other statistical software.</p>
<p>In Export 3D Points dialog check <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>To export Void points</b></span> option to store information and for the points that are outside the <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Max distance</i></span> range set in <a href="3D_Comparison.htm">Comparison</a> dialog.</p>
<p class="Code">The exported file contains table <span style="margin-left:40px;">of points with the following columns:</span></p>
<p class="Code"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Point X</b></span> - X co-ordinate of the point.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Point Y</b></span> - Y co-ordinate of the point.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Point Z</b></span> - Z co-ordinate of the point.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Reference X</b></span> - X co-ordinate of the closest position from the reference surface.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Reference Y</b></span> - Y co-ordinate of the closest position from the reference surface.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Reference Z</b></span> - Z co-ordinate of the closest position from the reference surface.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Distance X</b></span> - distance from the inspected point to the reference surface along Ox axis.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Distance Y</b></span> - distance from the inspected point to the reference surface along Oy axis.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Distance Z</b></span> - distance from the inspected point to the reference surface along Oz axis.<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
Distance</b></span> - distance from the inspected point to the reference surface.</p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> For Void points<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reference X</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reference Y</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reference Z</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Distance X</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Distance Y</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Distance Z</b></span>, and<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Distance</b></span> values are empty (marked with <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'-'</b></span> sign).</p>
<p>Formatting of the data is set-up from the <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; CSV File Export</b></i></span> dialog. KUBE uses the decimal symbol defined in Windows Regional Settings.</p>
